§ `Sections 245 to 248`

-- 245(3) the terms have the meanings of section 241.1
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(3) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 245(2) "Subsection (1) does not apply to (a) a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2; and (b) a person who does anything for the purpose of aiding ... to provide medical assistance in dying"
#ASSERT `s 245(2) subsection 245(1) applies to the person` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 245(2) subsection 245(1) applies to the person` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 245(2) subsection 245(1) applies to the person` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 245(2) subsection 245(1) applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 245(1) "Every person who administers or causes to be administered ... poison or any other destructive or noxious thing is guilty (a) of an indictable offence ... not exceeding fourteen years, if they did so with intent to endanger the life of or to cause bodily harm; or (b) ... two years, with intent to aggrieve or annoy"
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the person commits the offence of administering a noxious thing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the person commits the offence of administering a noxious thing` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the class of the offence` `s 245(1)(a) with intent to endanger the life of or to cause bodily harm to that person` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the class of the offence` `s 245(1)(b) with intent to aggrieve or annoy that person` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the punishment` `s 245(1)(a) with intent to endanger the life of or to cause bodily harm to that person` `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `s 245(1) the punishment` `s 245(1)(b) with intent to aggrieve or annoy that person` `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 246 "Every one who, with intent to enable or assist himself or another person to commit an indictable offence, (a) attempts, by any means, to choke, suffocate or strangle another person, or ... to render another person insensible, unconscious or incapable of resistance, or (b) administers ... a stupefying or overpowering drug, matter or thing, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life"
#ASSERT `s 246 the person commits the offence of overcoming resistance to commission of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246 the person commits the offence of overcoming resistance to commission of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246 the person commits the offence of overcoming resistance to commission of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 246 the person commits the offence of overcoming resistance to commission of an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 246 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 246 the punishment` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
-- 247(1) "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... five years ... summary conviction who with intent to cause death or bodily harm to a person, whether ascertained or not, (a) sets or places a trap, device or other thing that is likely to cause death or bodily harm to a person; or (b) being in occupation or possession of a place, knowingly permits such a trap ... to remain in that place"
--                                                                                  intent (a)   (b)
#ASSERT `s 247(1) the person commits the offence of setting a trap likely to cause bodily harm` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247(1) the person commits the offence of setting a trap likely to cause bodily harm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247(1) the person commits the offence of setting a trap likely to cause bodily harm` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(1) the person commits the offence of setting a trap likely to cause bodily harm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 247(1) the punishment` `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 247(2) "Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1), and by doing so causes bodily harm to any other person, is guilty of ... ten years ... or summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 247(2) the person commits the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247(2) the person commits the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(2) the person commits the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(2) the person commits the offence of setting a trap and causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 247(2) the punishment` `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 247(3) "Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1), in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence, is guilty of ... ten years ... or summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 247(3) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247(3) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(3) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 247(3) the punishment` `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 247 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 247(4) "Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1), in a place kept or used for the purpose of committing another indictable offence, and thereby causes bodily harm to a person is guilty of an indictable offence ... fourteen years"
#ASSERT `s 247(4) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place and causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247(4) the person commits the offence of setting a trap in an offence-related place and causing bodily harm` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
